  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Dump your Aces and Tens on tricks that OTHER players win. The goal is to stay 'under' the point threshold of the biggest loser of the round.\n\nDuck Tricks: Even if you could win a trick, sometimes it's better to play a low 7 or 8 to ensure you aren't forced to lead the next trick (which is always dangerous).\n\nThe Durchmarsch Gambit: If you hold 3+ Jacks and several Aces, you might try to win every single trick. This is high risk; if you miss even one trick, you will likely end up with the most points and take the penalty.",
    Player: "Dump your Aces and Tens on tricks that OTHER players win. The goal is to stay 'under' the point threshold of the biggest loser of the round.\n\nDuck Tricks: Even if you could win a trick, sometimes it's better to play a low 7 or 8 to ensure you aren't forced to lead the next trick (which is always dangerous).\n\nThe Durchmarsch Gambit: If you hold 3+ Jacks and several Aces, you might try to win every single trick. This is high risk; if you miss even one trick, you will likely end up with the most points and take the penalty.",
